<h3 id="customize-the-appearance">Customize the Appearance</h3>
<p>
	VetPress is a block theme, so you customize it in the Site Editor instead of the Customizer. Go to <strong>Appearance &gt; Editor</strong>:
</p>
<ul>
	<li><strong>Styles</strong> changes colors, fonts, spacing and the look of each block across the whole site, and switches between the <a href="#style-variations">style variations</a> under <strong>Browse styles</strong>.</li>
	<li><strong>Templates</strong> and <strong>Patterns</strong> change the layout of each kind of page and the shared header and footer. See <a href="#site-editor">Site Editor</a>.</li>
	<li><strong>Pages</strong> opens your pages, where each section is a pattern you can edit, move or delete. See <a href="#pages">Pages &amp; Patterns</a>.</li>
</ul>
